# Push-Review Skill

Apply after completing a reviewed fix (e.g. a Codex finding) that must be
delivered and re-reviewed on its pull request.

## 1. Commit

- One logical change per commit; conventional commit message
  (`fix:`, `feat:`, `refactor:`, `test:`, `docs:`, `chore:`).
- Stage only the files the fix touched — never `git add .`.
- Confirm the working tree is clean after committing.

## 2. Push

- Push the current branch: `git push origin <branch>`.
- If the push is rejected, fetch and rebase onto the updated remote; never
  rewrite pushed history unless replacing an accidental commit, and then only
  with lease protection (`git push --force-with-lease`).

## 3. Trigger Codex review

- `gh` CLI may be absent. Post a PR comment via the GitHub API instead:
  resolve the token with `git credential fill` (keychain), pipe it directly
  into `curl`, and never print or store it:

  ```
  cred=$(printf 'protocol=https\nhost=github.com\n' | git credential fill)
  token=$(printf '%s' "$cred" | sed -n 's/^password=//p')
  curl -s -X POST \
    -H "Authorization: Bearer $token" \
    -H 'Accept: application/vnd.github+json' \
    https://api.github.com/repos/<owner>/<repo>/issues/<pr>/comments \
    -d '{"body":"@codex review"}'
  ```

- Expect HTTP `201`; capture the returned comment URL and report it.

## 4. Report

In the final answer include: files changed, commit hash, push result
(before/after SHAs), the review-trigger URL, and verification results for
every gate that was run.
